  "question": {
    "text": "Which technique among the following, is most appropriate in separation of a mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mg</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>-nitrophenol and picric acid?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Steam distillation",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ft</mi></math> long column of silica gel",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Sublimation",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Preparative TLC (Thin Layer Chromatography)",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0182_b83390520781.png\" style=\"width: 317px; height: 300px;\" /></p><p>Solvent polarity has been related to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> value of nitrocompounds.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mg</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>-nitrophenol and picric acid have different <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> value on silica gel plate</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Preparative TLC is best to separate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mg</mi></math> of para nitrophenol and picric acid</p></blockquote>"
  }
